invariant: INV-14
file: srv.c
catches: tcp_blocking_loop_widemul
reason: ch_srv_check stops asking for the caller's answer, and signs with each
  identity under whatever byte the field holds, so a boot check passes a
  configuration every init call refuses. test/tcp_blocking_loop_widemul.h
  requires ch_srv_check to refuse 0 and 3 and to take each answer.

--- old
    // Both checks sign, under the multiply the caller's answer names.
    if (!widemul_answer_ok(cfg)) {
        return CH_EINVAL;
    }
--- new
    // Both checks sign, under the multiply the caller's answer names.
